                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to emeralds."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8c18a5ed-b5de-3dc7-98f9-72a11d01ee0c",
                        "entry_id": "c30f40a2-bdcf-3e3f-a4b8-ba719efc80fe",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having the colour of emeralds."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0b43517-3a9d-4e26-bd0c-a472442e1ec4",
                                "sense_id": "8c18a5ed-b5de-3dc7-98f9-72a11d01ee0c",
                                "text": "Not even inspired vision ever saw sweeter fields arrayed in living green than these spangled meads which stretch out for miles on either side, and probably lead to \"rivers of delight\" just beyond those massive banks of beech and oaken and maple foliage, which frame the view in smaragdine opulence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a296f967-1292-4891-9389-20b0e5cd425b",
                                "sense_id": "8c18a5ed-b5de-3dc7-98f9-72a11d01ee0c",
                                "text": "Under a smaragdine canopy of beeches, whose trunks, massive and fantastick, were sheathed in iron grey mail, the afternoon was warm."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7938777b-69cf-407c-b6ab-dfca13e45d46",
                                "sense_id": "8c18a5ed-b5de-3dc7-98f9-72a11d01ee0c",
                                "text": "[…] We will get the Hillbilly Woman very very high and she will lead us over the smaragdine mountain to a quiet pool where the Violent One awaits you.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "189c82e9-44d0-4d07-a555-f788a4a47657",
                                "sense_id": "8c18a5ed-b5de-3dc7-98f9-72a11d01ee0c",
                                "text": "She did not squint not as the sun crept through the Venetian blinds and seemed to ignite her already-luminous smaragdine eyes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "665a0711-9de2-443c-b8e0-ff546a32e041",
